---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Where the outcome of a run goes
    accDescr: A run, scheduled, by hand or a dry-run, writes its report. The status of the app keeps the state, the times and the report of the last run, which the settings page shows at every visit, the errors first. The error of a document goes to the Nextcloud log as a warning when it first occurs or changes. A run that changed something, and every import that Paperless finished, failed or refused, adds an entry to the Activity stream of the target user, with links to the files, but a dry-run adds none.

    run(["`⚙️ Run<br>*scheduled, by hand<br>or dry-run*`"])
    report["`📋 Report<br>*counts, up to 100 lines,<br>errors first*`"]
    status["`🗂️ Status<br>*state, times, errors<br>and report of the last run*`"]
    page["`🖥️ Settings page<br>*at every visit*`"]
    log["`📜 Nextcloud log<br>*a warning for each<br>new error of a document*`"]
    activity["`🔔 Activity stream<br>*of the target user: changes<br>and imports, with links*`"]

    run --> report --> status --> page
    run -- "errors" --> log
    run -- "changes, not of a dry-run" --> activity

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef warning fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class run,report,status,page,activity nextcloud
    class log warning
